# Parameter-naming style

Parameters are named with an "a" prefix, unless they start with a vowel (i.e., are pronounced beginning with a vowel sound), in which case they are named with a "an" prefix.

Class instance variables are named with a "my" prefix. Static (shared) class variables are named with an "our" prefix.

For example:

```java
public void setHex( Point aHex, anUpdateValue)
{
   myHex = aHex;
   myNewValue = anUpdateValue;
}
```

